{
  "name": "core-loop-visual",
  "description": "Visual verification of the full core gameplay loop: survey → drill plan → charge → sequence → blast → fragments → contract delivery. Multi-angle screenshots at each phase to confirm smooth transitions and visual feedback.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "command": "new_game seed:42 size:24",
      "timeout": 15,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "new_game seed:42 size:24"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000,
          "employeeCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow",
      "description": "campaign start replaces the site entirely with dusty_hollow's own fixed 96x96 grid -- new_game's size:24 above never actually takes effect once this runs.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "campaign start level:dusty_hollow"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 50000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "time resume",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "time resume"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup"
    },
    {
      "command": "employee hire role:surveyor",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"employees\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-employee-panel [data-role=\"surveyor\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"],
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1,
          "qualificationCount": 1,
          "proficiencyTotal": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:geology level:3",
      "description": "Corrected from bare positional args (`employee assign_skill 1 geology 3`), which the command silently rejects (`skill`/`level` are named params, per assignSkillCommand's own usage string) -- Finding #15's class, the same syntax bug caught earlier in survey-confidence-overlay.json. Left unmarked: hiring already grants the Rookie starting qualification (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION in Employee.ts); this only raises the level for the scenario's needs -- the player-facing path is `employee train`.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "employee assign_skill 1 skill:geology level:3"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 48800,
          "proficiencyTotal": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "survey seismic x:20 z:20",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"survey\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-survey-panel [data-method=\"seismic\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-survey-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "pickTile",
          "x": 20,
          "z": 20
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "decreased": ["cash"]
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "tick 5",
      "description": "Not long enough for the surveyor to walk to (20,20) and complete the survey (arrival-gated, #437) -- this file's own core-loop demonstration doesn't wait on it, moving straight to drilling instead.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "tick 5"
        }
      ],
      "role": "setup",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 45800,
          "surveyCount": 0
        },
        "note": "confirmed via direct trace: cash stays flat here -- with only 1 employee and no buildings/vehicles yet, payroll doesn't cycle within just 5 ticks"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "event choose 0",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "event choose 0"
        }
      ],
      "description": "event choose 0 -- follows a bare tick, so whether an event is pending is a random roll; there may be no dialog on screen. Deliberately left unmarked (Finding #15)."
    },
    {
      "command": "survey show",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "survey show"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "drill_plan grid rows:4 cols:4 spacing:3 depth:8 start:20,20",
      "description": "Corrected from the original rows:3 cols:3 spacing:5 (which command mode ran literally, producing 9 holes): the click drags the (20,20)-(30,30) rectangle at the Drill panel's own default spacing (DEFAULT_SPACING_M=3), computing cols/rows as round(size/spacing)+1 = 4x4 = 16 holes for that same rectangle -- the command and the click were silently testing two different grids, the same class of bug already fixed in nav-cell-types-visual.json. Caught by adding expect.equals.holeCount; fixed by describing what the click actually produces.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"blast\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"grid-tool\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        },
        {
          "type": "dragTiles",
          "x1": 20,
          "z1": 20,
          "x2": 30,
          "z2": 30
        },
        {
          "type": "screenshot"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-tile-select-confirm"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 16
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "charge hole:* explosive:boomite amount:5 stemming:2",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"charge-all\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "chargedCount": 16
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence auto delay_step:25",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"auto-sequence\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "sequencedCount": 16
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "sequence show",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "sequence show"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "blast_preview",
      "description": "This file never buys any software tier, so the preview prints '[Requires software tier N]' for every section (see safety-projection-visual.json for the unlocked version) -- still a real, clickable control either way.",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-step=\"4\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"run-analysis\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 45800
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "blast",
      "timeout": 20,
      "frames": 6,
      "interval": 50,
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-blast-panel [data-action=\"execute\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": ".bs-confirm-overlay .bs-btn-danger"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "[data-action=\"report-close\"]"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "holeCount": 0,
          "chargedCount": 0,
          "sequencedCount": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "fragments",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "fragments"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "contract list",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "contract list"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "contract accept 1",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-toolbar [data-panel=\"contracts\"]"
        },
        {
          "type": "waitForSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-contract-panel .bs-contract-accept"
        },
        {
          "type": "clickSelector",
          "selector": "#bs-contract-panel .bs-contract-accept"
        }
      ],
      "role": "player",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "activeContractCount": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "contract deliver 1 amount:500",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "contract deliver 1 amount:500"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Left unmarked (legacy): `contract deliver` returns success:false rather than throwing when the amount exceeds stock, and command-mode's runner only fails a step on a thrown exception, so the exact deliverable amount here is not independently verified. Same class as Finding #2. This file never hauls anything into storage -- like contract-negotiation.json, delivery genuinely fails every run (confirmed via direct trace: \"Not enough dirtite in storage: 0.0 kg available\").",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "cash": 45800,
          "activeContractCount": 1
        },
        "note": "the contract stays active/undelivered -- this file's own \"contract delivery\" step in its description is a queued attempt, not a completed one; economy-full-loop.json is the file that actually hauls stock and completes a delivery"
      }
    },
    {
      "command": "finances",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "finances"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "scores",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "scores"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe"
    },
    {
      "command": "state full",
      "interaction": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "state full"
        }
      ],
      "role": "observe",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "employeeCount": 1,
          "activeContractCount": 1,
          "holeCount": 0
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "shots": [
    {
      "name": "overview",
      "yaw": 0,
      "pitch": 45
    },
    {
      "name": "ground-level",
      "yaw": 90,
      "pitch": 10
    },
    {
      "name": "drill-holes",
      "yaw": 45,
      "pitch": 30
    },
    {
      "name": "birdseye",
      "yaw": 0,
      "pitch": 80
    }
  ]
}
